<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jagat Singh II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1734">1734</a>–<a href="/years/1751">1751</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jagat Singh II was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana">Maharana</a> of Mewar from 1734 to 1751. His reign saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> begin to exact regular tribute from Mewar, and he presided over the Hurda conference of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> rulers in 1734, which sought to unite them against Maratha incursions without lasting effect. A patron of painting and building, he built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-palace">Jag Niwas</a>, now the Lake Palace, on an island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-pichola">Lake Pichola</a> in the 1740s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jagat-singh-ii.jpg" alt="Jagat Singh II" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharana_Jagat_Singh_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
